# 2aea5f21892d429ca03289ff2da35812
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:97 8b98a474b8974af2b19bbdf37ae24f37
msgid "E-Mailing"
msgstr ""

# 2ffcd3463ea942478555cb0c5dbb63ea
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:99 c3e336568347449b93472d63bd3f7e5a
msgid "**Mailings in Galette are designed to work from the members list.**"
msgstr ""

# 6a2449424d4b4974ae288e8f192ade33
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:101 a60ad581540c40d887eab04c9d3c6872
msgid ""
"Direct mailing creation will work without problems, but members selection is "
"harder."
msgstr ""

# 5b51977f68d94771afc37946ef1cfe3f
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:103 a809e188570d444482bb2e4827c18e48
msgid ""
"From Galette, you can send mailings to a selection of members. Each sent "
"mailing is stored in order to be reused, so you can select a stored mailing "
"to be used as a template, retrieving selected members list, mailing subject "
"and contents."
msgstr ""

# d05b6978063e45ed86ffbe9e8ff7cf18
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:105 f0130c95beee48738c826f3423ab21a0
msgid ""
"To send a new mailing, select members from the list and then use the `Send "
"an email` button at the bottom of the list. If some of selected members does "
"not have an email address, Galette will propose you to print corresponding "
"labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:107 fee8912b511943e98f3af3683b1eb18c
msgid "Selected members for mailing"
msgstr ""

# d56d0ebb34c44e82be3386c79589514a
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:112 87cc0e7d0b704fb18458cee15abc3efa
msgid ""
"Selecting members in the list must be done on one page only. Filtering "
"features, as well as the possibility to display all members will be useful ;)"
msgstr ""

# b43af1a893334ebd8d2ffc9fd64c434f
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:116 e2b17c173a0c4c2ebd05590313327010
msgid "You can choose a sender for each mailing:"
msgstr ""

# d0819adda07749daa1dd20dd38761450
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:118 10d57d3a954149f695a730ffe5eaaaf8
msgid ""
"**from Galette preferences** (default value): this will use information "
"stored in preferences,"
msgstr ""

# eedcb1a13df34ab4b9badcd9491e4053
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:119 62ee949059e341e0bd9ec37a89574a87
msgid ""
"**current logged-in user**: will use the name and the email of the current "
"logged-in user (not available for super admin),"
msgstr ""

# 15b160e5918f4e38ac39d87263ae7db9
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:120 d0a3323d34854416a715e0cb6f409f7e
msgid "**other**: you can set any name and email address you want."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:122 5911a0d958db4013bf0ad2b85353dd9b
msgid "Sender selection"
msgstr ""

# 5725e99d780344e193a8a8f60be178df
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:127 1c03055339dc445f80b7aabacf1f85b9
msgid ""
"Once the subject has been filled, you can work on the contents. You can send "
"email in text only, or in HTML (keep in mind sending HTML messages by mail "
"is often not the way to go). A simple HTML WYSIWYG editor is provided."
msgstr ""

# 9964f2f45b8745348c9c2583f74b757c
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:129 cc36a9679dda4867861d087aae70eb12
msgid ""
"Once the HTML editor is enabled, the checkbox to handle HTML tags is "
"automatically checked, remember to check the box if you do not use the "
"editor but want to send HTML!"
msgstr ""

# daaacbf33ca54093bd54afeef42d7da0
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:131 65a15d1a272a4256bf3d73eefc9635ca
msgid ""
"Even if Galette is able to send HTML emails, this is discouraged. Messages "
"length will be way larger (for almost nothing), and some (like me!) read "
"their emails as text only. That is why Galette will **always** provide a "
"text version of HTML emails."
msgstr ""

# 5e374f097326472abbb0bfea92411b08
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:133 6e0436d8cdb1497fb62ade7b078443c8
msgid ""
"It is also possible to add attachements, just click on the `Browse` button "
"in that attachements section. If your browser is compatible, you can add "
"several files at once (using `Shift` and `Ctrl` keys). All attachements are "
"stored on disk, under a directory named with the mailing identifier "
"(automatically defined from database)."
msgstr ""

# b588f7c454ac4f23b6e558c821f1e581
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:136 85d0670ba88843cfb69f7cd69f5e88f3
msgid "`Preview` button let you preview your message before sending it."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:138 7f9ed32ac4bf42fca90e0f52d52d14f8
msgid "Preview message"
msgstr ""

# d02d0fac4ecb4741b4fc8b6ee4a240e9
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:143 d84bea617bed4b7bad6ac0308bc93d23
msgid ""
"Any started emailings will be stored in your session to be retrieved in the "
"future. An icon will be displayed in pages titles when a mailing is progress "
"and will provide a link to go to it."
msgstr ""

# 0bdf241274e2439f9055eb30c33f2f1e
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:145 56a0e8b3fed546dab7a89e9aa7bf1c9a
msgid ""
"If you want, you can cancel this mailing using the `Cancel mailing` button, "
"it will be deleted from your session. If you want to store it for a longer "
"time, you can add the `Save` button. It will then be stored in the mailings "
"list, and you will be able to grab it later."
msgstr ""

# dcc74c1381e443ff8db505aaa51d3c8e
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:148 9027c8f7745f4e379c3ff9cf26819cb6
msgid "Mailings history"
msgstr ""

# b564deab888641db99724c1d95bc1438
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:150 0925bc92c4984afcb34ac9c2174712e6
msgid ""
"When you start a mailing, it is stored into your session. Session ends when "
"users log out, or on a server defined timeout. Mailing history stores the "
"mailing in the database, this ensure it will always be available in the "
"future."
msgstr ""

# 114b440766e04f8cbde2bca533e0ebba
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:152 67d96e213ab24f949aadaaed23107b1b
msgid ""
"Every sent mailing is stored into the database, and can be used as a "
"template to write a new one. In this case, a new mailing will be created "
"using information from the history, and the original one will be kept as is."
msgstr ""

# 75ad268996ed4e0da907b51ea3fde96a
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:154 927d38f491d641f197a96b8ff00b3eda
msgid ""
"Mailings can be stored before they are sent. In this case, it is possible to "
"continue it later. When you use history on a draft mailing, original entry "
"will be replaced on sending."
msgstr ""

# 4b0e22297d5c4fb1bd80059de2cc1870
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:156 bb6cf3adaa8a4a2285caba5dc9dbdd40
msgid ""
"When you use an existing history entry, here are the information that will "
"be used:"
msgstr ""

# 3cb1f26280494c8986291bba1b241693
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:158 bd6db00975be42929b986ccff81f82f2
msgid "recipients,"
msgstr ""

# b635e2bce9294fcca3cd50c042776b31
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:159 a95c3f6e3f264a69bb3f4373747943c1
msgid "attachements,"
msgstr ""

# 3d8ab50c64374df8bd2c025d88fdf03e
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:160 225ac38201d44524a7672186a1f9b6ca
msgid "subject,"
msgstr ""

# c5de0398237446b7add2e64d38fa44f8
#: ../usermanual/adherents.rst:161 2dfa24ffd4b04e3c941375147a457f03
msgid "message,"
msgstr ""

# e36a2c5c3c5f4abc9602b892e7a91910
